# doq: kept in English by the translator (name or code)
#. type: Title ###
#, no-wrap
msgid "Motivation {#motivation}"
msgstr "Motivation {#motivation}"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Quantum Chromodynamics (QCD), the SU(3) gauge theory of the strong force, binds quarks into hadrons and governs confinement and string breaking. Classical lattice QCD methods excel at static properties but cannot simulate real-time dynamics due to the sign problem. Quantum computers offer a route around this barrier by encoding gauge field degrees of freedom directly onto qubits.\n"
msgstr "Kromodinamik Kuantum (QCD), teori gauge SU(3) bagi daya kuat, mengikat quark menjadi hadron dan mengawal kurungan dan pemecahan tali. Kaedah QCD kekisi klasik cemerlang dalam sifat statik tetapi tidak dapat mensimulasikan dinamik masa nyata disebabkan masalah tanda. Komputer kuantum menawarkan laluan untuk mengatasi halangan ini dengan mengekod darjah kebebasan medan gauge secara langsung ke atas Qubit.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "This tutorial demonstrates such a simulation: use IBM Quantum hardware to simulate real-time hadron propagation in a (1+1)-dimensional SU(2) lattice gauge theory &mdash; the simplest non-Abelian gauge theory and a stepping stone toward full QCD.\n"
msgstr "Tutorial ini menunjukkan simulasi sedemikian: menggunakan perkakasan IBM Quantum untuk mensimulasikan perambatan hadron masa nyata dalam teori gauge kekisi SU(2) (1+1)-dimensi &mdash; teori gauge bukan-Abelian yang paling mudah dan batu loncatan ke arah QCD penuh.\n"

# doq: kept in English by the translator (name or code)
#. type: Title ###
#, no-wrap
msgid "The Kogut-Susskind Hamiltonian {#the-kogut-susskind-hamiltonian}"
msgstr "The Kogut-Susskind Hamiltonian {#the-kogut-susskind-hamiltonian}"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "The theory is formulated on a 1D spatial lattice with staggered fermions (matter) on sites and SU(2) gauge fields on links. After rescaling to dimensionless form, the Hamiltonian is:\n"
msgstr "Teori ini dirumuskan pada kekisi ruang 1D dengan fermion tersusun-selang-seli (jirim) pada tapak dan medan gauge SU(2) pada pautan. Selepas penskalaan semula kepada bentuk tanpa dimensi, Hamiltonian ialah:\n"

# doq: copied, nothing translatable
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "$$W = H_E^{\\text{(KS)}} + \\mu H_M + x H_I^{\\text{(KS)}},$$\n"
msgstr "$$W = H_E^{\\text{(KS)}} + \\mu H_M + x H_I^{\\text{(KS)}},$$\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "where $H_E$ is the chromoelectric field energy, $H_M$ is the staggered mass term, $H_I$ is the matter-gauge interaction (hopping) term, $\\mu = 2\\frac{m}{g}\\sqrt{x}$ encodes the fermion mass, and $x = \\frac{1}{g^2 a^2}$ is the interaction strength. The continuum limit of the theory lies at $N \\to \\infty$ and $x \\to \\infty$.\n"
msgstr "di mana $H_E$ ialah tenaga medan kromoelektrik, $H_M$ ialah sebutan jisim tersusun-selang-seli, $H_I$ ialah sebutan interaksi jirim-gauge (hopping), $\\mu = 2\\frac{m}{g}\\sqrt{x}$ mengekod jisim fermion, dan $x = \\frac{1}{g^2 a^2}$ ialah kekuatan interaksi. Had kontinum bagi teori ini terletak pada $N \\to \\infty$ dan $x \\to \\infty$.\n"

# doq: kept in English by the translator (name or code)
#. type: Title ###
#, no-wrap
msgid "The Loop-String-Hadron (LSH) framework {#the-loop-string-hadron-lsh-framework}"
msgstr "The Loop-String-Hadron (LSH) framework {#the-loop-string-hadron-lsh-framework}"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "A key challenge is that the gauge field Hilbert space on each link is infinite-dimensional. The **Loop-String-Hadron (LSH)** framework addresses this by reformulating the theory in terms of gauge-invariant variables &mdash; loops of flux, strings connecting separated charges, and hadrons (gauge-singlet fermion pairs at a site). In the LSH basis, Gauss's law is satisfied automatically by construction, so every basis state is physical. Each lattice site is characterized by three quantum numbers $(n_l, n_i, n_o)$ representing the loop number, incoming string, and outgoing string, where $n_i, n_o \\in \\{0,1\\}$ are fermionic and $n_l \\geq 0$ is bosonic. The local fermion number is defined from these as $n_f(r) = n_i(r) + n_o(r)$ for even sites and $n_f(r) = 2 - [n_i(r) + n_o(r)]$ for odd sites.\n"
msgstr "Satu cabaran utama ialah ruang Hilbert medan gauge pada setiap pautan adalah tak terhingga dimensi. Rangka kerja **Loop-String-Hadron (LSH)** menangani ini dengan merumuskan semula teori dari segi pemboleh ubah tak varian-gauge &mdash; gelung fluks, tali yang menghubungkan cas terpisah, dan hadron (pasangan fermion singlet-gauge pada tapak). Dalam asas LSH, hukum Gauss dipenuhi secara automatik melalui pembinaan, jadi setiap keadaan asas adalah fizikal. Setiap tapak kekisi dicirikan oleh tiga nombor kuantum $(n_l, n_i, n_o)$ yang mewakili nombor gelung, tali masuk, dan tali keluar, di mana $n_i, n_o \\in \\{0,1\\}$ adalah fermionik dan $n_l \\geq 0$ adalah bosonik. Nombor fermion setempat ditakrifkan daripada ini sebagai $n_f(r) = n_i(r) + n_o(r)$ untuk tapak genap dan $n_f(r) = 2 - [n_i(r) + n_o(r)]$ untuk tapak ganjil.\n"

# doq: kept in English by the translator (name or code)
#. type: Title ###
#, no-wrap
msgid "From full Hamiltonian to the quantum circuit: three key approximations {#from-full-hamiltonian-to-the-quantum-circuit-three-key-approximations}"
msgstr "From full Hamiltonian to the quantum circuit: three key approximations {#from-full-hamiltonian-to-the-quantum-circuit-three-key-approximations}"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "The quantum circuit does **not** simulate the full SU(2) Hamiltonian exactly. Instead, it implements a controlled series of approximations that are valid in the **weak-coupling regime** ($x \\gg 1$). Understanding what is and is not approximated is essential:\n"
msgstr "Circuit kuantum **tidak** mensimulasikan Hamiltonian SU(2) penuh dengan tepat. Sebaliknya, ia mengimplementasikan siri anggaran terkawal yang sah dalam **rejim gandingan lemah** ($x \\gg 1$). Memahami apa yang dianggarkan dan tidak dianggarkan adalah penting:\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "**Approximation 1 &mdash; Weak-coupling limit for $H_I$:** The full interaction Hamiltonian $H_I^{\\text{(LSH)}}$ (Eq. 16 in [[1]](#references)) contains prefactors that depend on the bosonic quantum number $n_l$ via terms like $1/\\sqrt{n_l+1}$. In the weak-coupling regime ($x \\gg 1$), the dynamics is dominated by the electric term $H_E$, which favors states with large $n_l$. For $n_l \\gg 1$, the ratio $n_l/(n_l+1) \\to 1$ and all these prefactors simplify to unity. The interaction Hamiltonian then reduces to a purely local nearest-neighbor hopping:\n"
msgstr "**Anggaran 1 &mdash; Had gandingan lemah untuk $H_I$:** Hamiltonian interaksi penuh $H_I^{\\text{(LSH)}}$ (Pers. 16 dalam [[1]](#references)) mengandungi prapemberat yang bergantung kepada nombor kuantum bosonik $n_l$ melalui sebutan seperti $1/\\sqrt{n_l+1}$. Dalam rejim gandingan lemah ($x \\gg 1$), dinamik didominasi oleh sebutan elektrik $H_E$, yang menggemari keadaan dengan $n_l$ yang besar. Untuk $n_l \\gg 1$, nisbah $n_l/(n_l+1) \\to 1$ dan semua prapemberat ini dipermudahkan kepada satu. Hamiltonian interaksi kemudian tereduksi kepada hopping jiran-terdekat setempat semata-mata:\n"

# doq: copied, nothing translatable
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "$$H_I^{\\text{approx}} = -\\sum_r \\left[\\sigma^-(r)\\sigma^+(r+1) + \\sigma^+(r)\\sigma^-(r+1)\\right],$$\n"
msgstr "$$H_I^{\\text{approx}} = -\\sum_r \\left[\\sigma^-(r)\\sigma^+(r+1) + \\sigma^+(r)\\sigma^-(r+1)\\right],$$\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "which is independent of $n_l$ and acts only on the fermionic $(n_i, n_o)$ qubits.\n"
msgstr "yang tidak bergantung kepada $n_l$ dan hanya bertindak pada Qubit fermionik $(n_i, n_o)$.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "**Approximation 2 &mdash; Global-average-flux for $H_E$:** The electric energy depends on $n_l$ at each link. In the weak-coupling vacuum, $n_l$ is large and approximately uniform. Replace the site-dependent $n_l$ values with a single global average $\\bar{n}_l$, making $H_E$ a diagonal phase proportional to the fermion configuration at each site:\n"
msgstr "**Anggaran 2 &mdash; Fluks-purata-global untuk $H_E$:** Tenaga elektrik bergantung kepada $n_l$ pada setiap pautan. Dalam vakum gandingan lemah, $n_l$ adalah besar dan lebih kurang seragam. Gantikan nilai $n_l$ yang bergantung tapak dengan satu purata global tunggal $\\bar{n}_l$, menjadikan $H_E$ satu fasa pepenjuru berkadar dengan konfigurasi fermion pada setiap tapak:\n"

# doq: copied, nothing translatable
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "$$H_E^{\\text{approx}} = N h_E^0 + \\sum_{\\{r'\\}} \\left(\\frac{\\bar{n}_l}{2} + \\frac{3}{4}\\right)$$\n"
msgstr "$$H_E^{\\text{approx}} = N h_E^0 + \\sum_{\\{r'\\}} \\left(\\frac{\\bar{n}_l}{2} + \\frac{3}{4}\\right)$$\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "where $\\{r'\\}$ sums over sites in the fermionic configuration $(n_i=0, n_o=1)$, and $h_E^0$ is a global phase you can ignore.\n"
msgstr "di mana $\\{r'\\}$ menjumlahkan ke atas tapak dalam konfigurasi fermionik $(n_i=0, n_o=1)$, dan $h_E^0$ ialah fasa global yang boleh anda abaikan.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "**Approximation 3 &mdash; Trotterization:** The time-evolution operator for a step of duration $\\delta_\\tau$ is decomposed as:\n"
msgstr "**Anggaran 3 &mdash; Trotterization:** Operator evolusi masa untuk satu langkah bertempoh $\\delta_\\tau$ diuraikan sebagai:\n"

# doq: copied, nothing translatable
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "$$e^{-i\\delta_\\tau W} \\approx e^{-i\\tilde{m} H_M} \\, e^{-i\\delta_\\tau H_E^{\\text{approx}}} \\, e^{-ic H_I^{\\text{approx}}}$$\n"
msgstr "$$e^{-i\\delta_\\tau W} \\approx e^{-i\\tilde{m} H_M} \\, e^{-i\\delta_\\tau H_E^{\\text{approx}}} \\, e^{-ic H_I^{\\text{approx}}}$$\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "where $c = \\delta_\\tau x$, $\\tilde{m} = \\delta_\\tau \\mu$, and $\\theta = -\\delta_\\tau(\\bar{n}_l/2 + 3/4)$. This first-order Trotter decomposition introduces an error that vanishes as $\\delta_\\tau \\to 0$. We fix $\\delta_\\tau = 0.0015$ throughout.\n"
msgstr "di mana $c = \\delta_\\tau x$, $\\tilde{m} = \\delta_\\tau \\mu$, dan $\\theta = -\\delta_\\tau(\\bar{n}_l/2 + 3/4)$. Penguraian Trotter tertib pertama ini memperkenalkan ralat yang hilang apabila $\\delta_\\tau \\to 0$. Kita menetapkan $\\delta_\\tau = 0.0015$ sepanjang.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "**The result** of these three approximations is that only the two fermionic qubits per site $(n_i, n_o)$ are dynamical &mdash; the bosonic $n_l$ degree of freedom has been absorbed into effective parameters. This yields a compact circuit with $2N$ qubits for $N$ lattice sites, where each Trotter step has constant two-qubit gate depth (13 per step).\n"
msgstr "**Hasil** ketiga-tiga anggaran ini ialah hanya kedua-dua Qubit fermionik setiap tapak $(n_i, n_o)$ yang dinamik &mdash; darjah kebebasan bosonik $n_l$ telah diserap ke dalam parameter berkesan. Ini menghasilkan Circuit padat dengan $2N$ Qubit untuk $N$ tapak kekisi, di mana setiap langkah Trotter mempunyai kedalaman gate dua-qubit tetap (13 setiap langkah).\n"

# doq: kept in English by the translator (name or code)
#. type: Title ###
#, no-wrap
msgid "What this tutorial simulates {#what-this-tutorial-simulates}"
msgstr "What this tutorial simulates {#what-this-tutorial-simulates}"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "The tutorial simulates **hadron propagation**: starting from the strong-coupling vacuum (a product state), place a meson at the center of the lattice and evolve in time. The differential measurement protocol &mdash; running the circuit with and without the central meson, then subtracting &mdash; isolates the coherent hadron signal from both hardware noise and boundary effects. The result is a light-cone pattern of fermion density oscillations characteristic of a confined meson breathing mode.\n"
msgstr "Tutorial ini mensimulasikan **perambatan hadron**: bermula daripada vakum gandingan kuat (keadaan hasil darab), letakkan satu meson di tengah kekisi dan berevolusi dalam masa. Protokol pengukuran pembezaan &mdash; menjalankan Circuit dengan dan tanpa meson tengah, kemudian menolak &mdash; mengasingkan isyarat hadron koheren daripada kedua-dua hingar perkakasan dan kesan sempadan. Hasilnya ialah corak kon-cahaya bagi ayunan ketumpatan fermion yang menjadi ciri mod pernafasan meson terkurung.\n"

